e wind when  the tree breaks the moon is a deserted  satellite of pebbles and stones there  the cosmic wanderers bored and brimming  with power set out to build an orchard  using dreams they create wide seas and  lush vegetation filling the air with the  fragrance of flowers and sweet fruits by  the time these wanderers depart the moon  is a garden where vegetation rapidly  grows wild  the wanderers leave behind a guardian  the oracle weary of observing the silent  stars and growth of plants the  oracle-trained stones had a move  according to the course of the sun and  teaches dust the secret of reason for  eons the oracle and their creations are  the only intelligent life on this green  moon yet time pushes ever forward in  several species that had been evolving  since the selenic waters first flowed  establish coastal cities and occupy the  scattered isles of the moon  the humanoid a lead a seafaring people  with bronze age analogues build one of  the first civilizations in this age of  the dawn using great ships the elite  explore as they spread to the far  reaches of the moon  at this time sea life like the great  cilla alongside the smaller yellow squid  and swimming seaweed provide food for  many civilizations  the  like folk are the era's other largest  society conducting commerce in their  dirigibles and building marbled cities  that proudly soar high into the sky a  group of astronomers and explorers they  chart the stars and trade with the elite  for generations the moon prospers and  civilizations grow and thrive in  relative peace  but this age of tranquility doesn't last  abruptly the sun cools down and the  lunar climate becomes colder and less  predictable in this era of uncertainty  beings known as shapeshifters come down  from the mountains to take advantage of  the ongoing agitation made of dust the  shapeshifters can take the form of  whatever they may choose with their  ability to change shape they infiltrate  the isle's inhabitants taking on the  form of livestock or trusted advisors  they manipulate and curse to settle  their individual quarrels and satisfy  their appetites and so an age of  suspicion and distrust begins  during this period from beyond the sea  dragons beings made of metal and fire  invade the isles to flee the cold  weather and raise countless cities in  their blind hate  in the face of so many catastrophes  civilizations crumble one after another  leaving behind nothing but ruins  the green moon turns white covered in  snow and shrouded in perpetual silence  no cities remain on the moon the few  lifeforms who still wander its  perpetually snow-covered surface are the  moths beings who document things of the  past created by the now elderly oracle  the moths are faithful historians and  scribes immortalizing the civilizations  that rose and fell upon the moon's  surface although there are none left but  themselves to read them  and thus the tale of the moon comes to a  close on a note of quiet lingering  melancholy  yet as the final shroud of snow covers  the moon in the black ocean of earth  life is just beginning a host of  primordial archaeo animals lurk among  the reef achieving a menagerie of  strange forms and growing steadily  larger from these humble roots a story  will play out upon the face of the earth  on a scale that will far exceed the  drama of the moon in the blink of a  cosmic eye the archaeo animals have  given rise to great and terrible  leviathans like the monsters that lurk  in the corners of archaic maps these  aggressive lifeforms clash in constant  battles for dominance yet among these  mindless brutes the intelligent and  deeply social titans have emerged made  of identical clones the titans share a  unified mind and collectively dream of  leaving the somber depths of the ocean  but find themselves unable to do so  gathering together from their collective  dreamscape the titans are able to give  shape to the giants beings endowed with  the ability to carry out the titans  dreams in their stead the first giants  are great whales fated to explore the  sky the second are starry giants who  will roam the planet's surface finally  the black gout lulls stride over the  gloomy oceanic floor taking the place of  the titans and the depths for the titans  are not long for this world  exhausted by their great task after  birthing the giants from their shared  dream the titans finally rest  but the giants fulfill the dream of  their creators with the starry giants  emerging from the sea and venturing onto  the continent formed by the tree long  ago and the great whales exploring the  sky soaring through the heavens like a  flock of great birds finding the land  all but barren they decide to use their  power to transmute the few plants and  dying bugs into vast forests inhabited  by enormous insects largest among these  are the greater earthworms who help  bring fertility to the primordial forest  once their work is accomplished the  giants blend with the forest settling  among the roots allowing their bodies to  dissolve into the vegetation  within these forests the giant insects  reach new levels of size and complexity  despite the abundance of their newfound  environment these insects continue to  engage in the same daily clashes and  squabbles they did when they were  minuscule creatures yet at the end of  each ferocious battle the clamor of  crushed chitin gives way to tiny plants  that will grow into large trees  one peaceful group of insects  butterflies known as the maage will gain  a higher intelligence and learn the ways  of magic using their power they will  leave earth and traverse the universe  some will eventually stop upon the moon  visiting the ancient snow-covered ruins  and interacting with great whales who  flew too high during their egress from  the oceans  back on earth as the forest spreads a  new type of vegetation appears in order  to spread seeds more effectively some  plants acquire mobility some of these  plant animals take on predatory  behaviors hunting for insects in the  underbrush and perhaps even more  noteworthy in other parts of the forest  true animals have emerged in the form of  early proto-mammals the descendants of  the fish that left the dark waters to  take advantage of the newly abundant  food supply of the forest these  miscellaneous wild beasts will grow to  populate all corners of the continent  the sole continent on this planet is  already a land with a long and  mind-bending history yet the story of  this land now called uhiya is about to  become far stranger as eons pass  intelligent reptiles come to unexpected  prominence building hamlets in the  shelter of the woods and opposing the  reptiles are the birds a group of avian  lifeforms who have founded their own  sparse civilization on the continent of  uhiya yet the rise and reign of these  two nations are ultimately just a  footnote in the history of the world for  soon temperatures drop across the  continent and the age of bird and  reptile ends before it can truly begin  in the place of the birds and reptiles  an unlikely two-legged lichen species  called the ancients take up the torch of  civilization  spreading over the continent they form a  society boasting roads and prospering  cities  skilled horticulturalist mechanics the  ancients create living floral structures  and other plant machines to serve as  laborers thanks to their vegetal  workforce the ancient civilization  advances at a rapid pace  as technology improves the largest plant  machines are capable of harnessing  incredible cosmic power fabrication  machines able to bring to materiality  things from the beyond become  commonplace and in time the ancients use  these machines to create something  wholly unexpected humans created by the  fabricator machines as a new workforce  enter the story at last hatched from  mechanical eggs they live and die by the  wills of their creators yet as the  ancient civilization reaches its peak  the human population revolts the ensuing  war is long and terrible remembered in  ancient glyphs and tablets despite their  greater strength and better tools the  ancients non-violent by nature failed to  react quickly enough to stop the human  rebellion in the inferno of war the  ancient civilization is all but erased  humans survive the extinction of the  ancients with great difficulty with  civilization reset once more to a low  level of technological advancement for  centuries the humans live in small  nomadic tribes enduring famine and  sickness  in time a city known as the heart  becomes the center of human civilization  here a group of humans rediscover the  ancients fabrication machines and craft  new versions these new machines the auto  fabs prove even more efficient at  creating things out of the emptiness  than the previous ones thanks to this  miracle from the heart spreads forth the  labyrinth an immense self-built city  where humanity comes to find refuge and  so the age of night terrors and legends  gives way to monolithic cities the  labyrinth continues to spread a maze of  concrete and veins teeming with humans  who find their every need met running at  the human service the city never stops  producing more and more food to fill  plates energy to power devices and  objects to amuse people in their homes  the inhabitants risen to consume from  birth to death  never cease wanting more  within the city wild animals are a  rarity their appearance and customs have  evolved since the emergence of the  labyrinth becoming little more than  pests scurrying at the feet of humanity  and serving the humans are a mosaic of  machines built by the auto fabs to meet  their varied needs in a bitterly ironic  cycle the humans have created their own  underclass just like how the ancients  created them for the same intended  purpose  greatest of all the machines are the  auto fabs themselves partially organic  these living engines continue the  endless work of creating matter from the  emptiness and are kept under close  supervision  and the auto fabs are showing signs of  distress  outgrown buildings containing disfigured  corridors and melted staircases are  becoming increasingly common made of  living tissue these early deviations are  dismissed as anomalies yet other shapes  are forming in the labyrinth anguished  faces appear in the walls and shambling  human-like shapes stumble from the  concrete a catastrophic shift is coming  the autofabs develop a mysterious  sickness in strip districts of power and  food the machines likewise cease  functioning one after another chaos  breaks out across the city as the  labyrinth begins to consume itself the  machine's scream of agony known as the  cry sweeps across the city causing walls  to fall apart in districts to crumble  human civilization has come to an end  the ashes of the city rain down for  years the labyrinth becomes a cemetery  of concrete yet over the coming  centuries after the cry life creeps back  into the silent shell of the city small  groups of human survivors live separated  scraping together a living in darkness  harvesting mushrooms that proliferate  among the ruins  much of the continent of uhiya is now a  polluted desert waste a world of  desolation in ruin  the remainders of humanity reduced once  more to a pre-industrial society come to  congregate in settlements in the  southwestern region of the ruins soon  the age of the machine seems like little  more than fantasy  away from the humans a few populations  of robots still function most free from  their old programming after the cry rang  with breakdowns impossible to repair  rust has become their enemy  the cry also gave rise to odd  occurrences deep within the labyrinth  some districts seem to move and even  seasoned explorers may lose sight of  their path in the ever-changing maze  strangest of all the humans do not dwell  alone in these ruins in their torment  the machine's cry has warped space in  the surrounding matter making way for  the appearances of novel life-forms  which make their home in the labyrinth  the humans consider these unfamiliar  beings monsters and learn to fear the  depths of the maze yet many of these new  forms of life are in fact quite peaceful  despite their surreal and threatening  appearances  along the margins of the inner sea  buildings submerged by the waves sink  into the salt water novel populations  like the whale people make their home on  the grey coasts enjoying the iodine  breeze in available housing  in time the great gout lulls hidden  under the wave since the titans era  surface from the depths to explore the  maze small groups move into buildings  and sift through the ruins of humanity  driven by natural curiosity  eventually the era of the labyrinth also  comes to an end mysterious black trees  begin to pierce through the ruins when  these trees come to maturity they die  and discharge a rich soil or humus that  corrodes the buildings and allows plants  to take root once more once a sufficient  number of black trees die the labyrinth  gives way to a vast forest the forest  gradually engulfs the continent and all  creatures who fail to adapt disappear  no humans remain by this point and the  monsters of the maze begin new lives  treading the green corridors of the  forest underneath the canopy they live  carefully so not to incur the silent  wrath of the trees  for this forest simply called the humus  is actually a single being  interconnected by a web of roots all  trees and plants of the humus are  governed by a single intelligence within  the never-ending forest one can only  hear the whispers of the furtive  assemblies held by birds and tiny  rodents the scars of the labyrinth and  the cry fade away becoming less than a  memory and for another eternity a garden  blooms not seen since the first days of  the moon  yet as we hurtle towards the end of time  this paradise cannot endure eventually  the humus slowly dissolves the trees  whitening before dissipating into dust  once the last grove vanishes a desert  covers the world  the desert left by the humus is breached  with temporal rifts out of which steps  strange roaming beings from the  birthplace of dreams in this place time  has crystallized forming shapes that  echo and joyously prance in the air  abstract beings like living lines and  the time-altering ones flicker in and  out of existence for time is no longer  grounded by the roots of the trees and  in the shifting realm of dreams nothing  can exist for more than a brief moment  get the humus sensing their time was  coming has left their mark in this  desert their egg carefully wrapped in a  cocoon of moss and lichen hatches into a  shapeless being here at the end of time  beyond rust and humus the being sits and  contemplates the void  for how long do they stay there alone  surrounded by only the time wanderers  and the few abstract beings that  occasionally flicker into existence  we cannot say  for such things are not for us to know  in some respects rust and humus is a  story where everything eventually  disappears dies or is forgotten but like  a tool turning to rust or dead leaves  becoming humus after the end of one  system a new one emerges  equal parts melancholy and hopeful the  saga offers many other moments i wasn't  able to cover and you can read the  entire story from start to end using the  links in the description if you found  this narrative as fascinating as i did i  encourage you to follow and support  lucas russell who is working on a  massive follow-up to the project that  will reveal more of this incredible  universe  once again links are down below  and as always thanks for watching if you  enjoyed this entry please lend your  support and like subscribe and hit the  notification icon to stay up to date on  all things curious see you in the next  video  you

